cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this ontology, please cite it as below."
title: "NuProc Ontology"
abstract: >-
  An OWL 2 ontology, SKOS vocabularies and SHACL shapes for engagement events in
  nuclear new-build procurement, kept apart from the news reports, coded records
  and coding claims through which they are known. A real-world layer of
  engagements and of the roles organisations bear in a procurement case and
  realize in its engagements, aligned to BFO and RO, is separated from an information layer of records, clusters, actor
  references with their resolution status, and claim-level coding provenance;
  only a cluster whose reported occurrence status is occurred reports an
  engagement or grounds a role.
type: software
version: "0.9.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/bonjwanim/nuprockg"
keywords:
  - ontology
  - knowledge graph
  - public procurement
  - nuclear energy
  - event data
  - provenance
  - SHACL
  - SKOS
  - roles
  - reference resolution
authors:
  - family-names: "Park"
    given-names: "Wonbae"
